reviews.text:
Expressing my concern about the insulin I received from Village Vets Rathfarnham on 17/11/2025. When I opened the package at home, I noticed several issues that are concerning for both safety and quality:
The box was not sealed;
The insulin vial was missing the red cap;
The quantity of insulin appeared to be less than expected;
The medication description inside the box did not correspond to the medication and was crumpled;
Given that this medication is essential for my pet’s health, receiving it in this condition was extremely worrying.
I would like to understand how this could have happened and what steps will be taken to prevent this from occurring again.
After I sent to them this message, they returned with this:

Thank you for bringing this to our attention. The bottles of prozinc do not come sealed, so this is not a quality issue. However the bottle should have had the red cap on it.
The boxes of insulin that we receive don't come with a tamper seal on them. We will take this observation and feedback on board and inquire with our supplier as to the reason why.

Village Vets@DSPCA
